.TH "HED-COPILOT" "1" "2026-08-23" "hed v1.21.3" "hed manual"
.SH NAME
hed\-copilot \- GitHub Copilot ghost\-text suggestions via the official
\[at]github/copilot\-language\-server JSON\-RPC server.
.PP
GitHub Copilot ghost\-text suggestions via the official
\f[CR]\[at]github/copilot\-language\-server\f[R] JSON\-RPC server.
.SH Install
The plugin spawns the language server as a child process.
Either:
.IP
.EX
npm install \-g \[at]github/copilot\-language\-server
.EE
.PP
\[em] in which case the \f[CR]copilot\-language\-server\f[R] shim ends
up on \f[CR]$PATH\f[R] and the plugin uses it automatically \[em] or
install it locally inside the project
(\f[CR]./node_modules/\[at]github/copilot\-language\-server/\f[R]),
which is also auto\-detected.
To override, set \f[CR]HED_COPILOT_LSP\f[R] to either a binary or a
\f[CR].js\f[R] file path.
.SH Sign in
.IP
.EX
:copilot login              \-> prints a userCode and a verification URL
:copilot login <userCode>   \-> confirm after entering the code in the browser
:copilot status             \-> show signed\-in user and enable state
:copilot logout
.EE
.PP
GitHub stores the OAuth token in
\f[CR]\[ti]/.config/github\-copilot/\f[R]; future sessions reconnect
without re\-logging\-in.
.SH How it behaves
.IP \[bu] 2
Once signed in, every char insert in INSERT mode at end\-of\-line
schedules a debounced (250 ms) \f[CR]getCompletions\f[R] request.
.IP \[bu] 2
The first returned completion renders as ghost text on the current row
using the \f[CR]copilot\f[R] virtual\-text namespace.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]<Tab>\f[R] in INSERT mode accepts the suggestion.
With no live suggestion, it falls back to inserting a literal tab (or
spaces, if \f[CR]expand_tab\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
Cursor move off the suggestion\[cq]s anchor row, or leaving INSERT mode,
dismisses it (and notifies the server with \f[CR]notifyRejected\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
Suggestions only render at end\-of\-line in v1; mid\-line ghost text
needs the inline placement form of virtual_text (currently EOL\-only).
.SH Alternatives pane
.IP
.EX
:copilot pane    \-> open a horizontal split listing all alternatives
:copilot next    \-> show the next alternative as the active ghost
:copilot prev    \-> show the previous alternative
.EE
.PP
The \f[CR][copilot]\f[R] buffer in the bottom pane refreshes on every
new response.
The active alternative is marked with \f[CR]*\f[R] at the start of its
line.
.SH Other commands
.IP
.EX
:copilot enable | disable    \-> toggle ghost\-text fetching
:copilot restart             \-> kill the server and respawn
.EE
.SH Implementation notes
.IP \[bu] 2
The plugin reuses the bundled \f[CR]cJSON\f[R] from
\f[CR]plugins/lsp/cjson/\f[R].
Framing (\f[CR]Content\-Length: \&...\f[R] LSP\-style headers) mirrors
\f[CR]plugins/lsp/lsp_impl.c\f[R].
.IP \[bu] 2
The \f[CR]copilot\f[R] virtual\-text namespace opts out of edit\-time
auto clearing (see \f[CR]vtext_ns_set_auto_clear\f[R]); the plugin
manages its own clears so ghost text survives the keystroke that
triggered the request.
.IP \[bu] 2
Document positions are sent as byte offsets (matching the editor\[cq]s
cursor.x).
Strict UTF\-16 code\-unit math is a v2 concern; ASCII files are the
common case.
.IP \[bu] 2
v1 sends a fresh \f[CR]doc.source\f[R] with every
\f[CR]getCompletions\f[R] and a \f[CR]textDocument/didOpen\f[R] per
buffer at sign\-in time; full incremental \f[CR]didChange\f[R] is
deferred.
